[{:seon.task/name "an-interrupt-leaves-nothing-pending"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `seon.intr`'s pending atom is set when root's interrupt finds no eval to stop and cleared only by `seon.intr/clear-pending!`, which the nREPL interrupt op (`seon.repl`) calls and root's `seon.root/interrupt!` (SIGUSR1) never sends; a set pending makes `seon.intr/run` start stopped. Reproduction (jolt/wiki 8c50215, through the server; re-verify first): after `seon.root/interrupt!` stopped `(loop [] (recur))` with \"interrupted by root\", every later eval in that agent bounded by :timeout-ms 200 (and in its clone) answered \"interrupted by root\" in 0.3 ms instead of running to its bound. Not traced: why pending was set although an eval was running when SIGUSR1 came. Correct: an interrupt ends exactly the form it reached; with no form running it is recorded as a no-op, and nothing carries into the next form or into a clone. Deletes the pending carry-over."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.intr-test/an-interrupt-ends-only-the-form-it-reached seon.intr-test/a-clone-starts-with-nothing-pending}}]
